{
  "wireMagic": "pb3",
  "pens": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wsWinStyles": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wpWinPositions": [ {
  
  } ],
  "events": [ {
    "tStartMs": 0,
    "dDurationMs": 4250,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "About 42,000 years ago,\nsomething happened on Earth"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 4274,
    "dDurationMs": 3930,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and it looked like the\nsky was breaking apart."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 9120,
    "dDurationMs": 3124,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "There were terrible\nlightning storms all around,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 12269,
    "dDurationMs": 3586,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and colourful auroras\nwere visible everywhere."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 15880,
    "dDurationMs": 4860,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Radiation from space reached\nEarth, destroying the ozone layer."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 21140,
    "dDurationMs": 3060,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Ultraviolet radiation\nincreased rapidly, and"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 24225,
    "dDurationMs": 3435,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a wave of climate change\ncame over the world."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 29740,
    "dDurationMs": 2920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This was a time when humans\nlived in jungles and caves."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 32660,
    "dDurationMs": 7000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "At this time, cave art made by the\nnatives was suddenly gaining popularity."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 39660,
    "dDurationMs": 3840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Scientists believe that\ndue to increasing ultraviolet"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 43524,
    "dDurationMs": 3544,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "radiation, humans used\nthese caves as shelters."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 47100,
    "dDurationMs": 3560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And during this time, many\nspecies became completely extinct."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 50660,
    "dDurationMs": 2988,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In Australia, giant\nkangaroos and giant wombats,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 53672,
    "dDurationMs": 2988,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "like these pictured here,\ncompletely disappeared."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 56660,
    "dDurationMs": 4900,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In Europe, the humanly species, \nNeanderthals, was also wiped out,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 61585,
    "dDurationMs": 3650,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "called the closest\nrelatives of Homo sapiens."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 65260,
    "dDurationMs": 2873,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But the question is,\nwhat happened on Earth?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 68340,
    "dDurationMs": 3780,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Its answer was not in\nthe sky, but under our feet,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 72660,
    "dDurationMs": 3759,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "hidden at a depth of\nabout 3,000 kilometres."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 76467,
    "dDurationMs": 4093,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And today, in 2026, something\nstrange is happening at this depth,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 80560,
    "dDurationMs": 4048,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the signs of which are now\nvisible even above the Earth."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 84633,
    "dDurationMs": 3264,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The region between South\nAmerica and Africa is where"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 87921,
    "dDurationMs": 3712,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "data from telescopes like\nthe Hubble is showing glitches."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 91633,
    "dDurationMs": 3593,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The equipment in the satellites\nis malfunctioning, and some"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 95251,
    "dDurationMs": 2869,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "systems have to be\nshut down for weeks"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 98120,
    "dDurationMs": 2000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to prevent them\nfrom deteriorating."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 100120,
    "dDurationMs": 4622,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That is why this area is called\nthe Bermuda Triangle of space."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 104767,
    "dDurationMs": 3353,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Let's understand this topic\nin depth in today's video."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 113646,
    "dDurationMs": 2814,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "First of all, I hope\nyou had a happy diwali."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 116460,
    "dDurationMs": 3720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This Diwali, focus on your\neducation and skill development."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 120180,
    "dDurationMs": 1240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Learn something new."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 121420,
    "dDurationMs": 1360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Increase your knowledge."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 122780,
    "dDurationMs": 2300,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And give yourself\nthe gift of a new skill."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 125080,
    "dDurationMs": 1800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "To help you with this,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 126880,
    "dDurationMs": 3360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Dhruv Rathee Academy is\nhaving a Mega Diwali Sale."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 130240,
    "dDurationMs": 4520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You will get a flat 50% off\non all my recorded courses."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 134760,
    "dDurationMs": 3200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That means you get a chance to learn\nyour favourite skill at half the price."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 137960,
    "dDurationMs": 2660,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If you want to make a\ncareer in social media,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 140620,
    "dDurationMs": 1780,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "or want to start a\nYouTube channel,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 142400,
    "dDurationMs": 2300,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "then you have the\nYouTube Blueprint course."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 144700,
    "dDurationMs": 3440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In this, you learn everything from\nplanning, scripting, filming, and editing."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 148140,
    "dDurationMs": 2900,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If you are suffering from\nprocrastination in your life,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 151040,
    "dDurationMs": 2280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and you want to\nachieve your goals better,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 153320,
    "dDurationMs": 2200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and manage your\ndaily life better,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 155520,
    "dDurationMs": 2820,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "then you have the Master\nTime Management course."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 158340,
    "dDurationMs": 2060,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Or to learn the\nfundamentals of AI,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 160400,
    "dDurationMs": 2200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you can choose the\nMaster ChatGPT course."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 162600,
    "dDurationMs": 2600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You get lifetime access\nto all these courses."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 165200,
    "dDurationMs": 2740,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Learn on your own time and watch\nthem again whenever you want."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 167940,
    "dDurationMs": 3300,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And along with this, there\nis a great sale on AI Fiesta."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 171240,
    "dDurationMs": 2160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This is an all in one\nAI app that gives"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 173400,
    "dDurationMs": 2160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you access to more\nthan 100 AI models."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 175560,
    "dDurationMs": 3840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Meaning, one platform to\naccess every AI tool in the world."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 179400,
    "dDurationMs": 3240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Whether it is to make photos,\nvideos, slides, websites, etc."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 182640,
    "dDurationMs": 2400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You can find the link to all of\nthese in the pinned comment below."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 185040,
    "dDurationMs": 2480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Or you can scan\nthis QR code as well."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 187520,
    "dDurationMs": 3960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But hurry up, because this is\nvalid only for a few days after Diwali."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 191480,
    "dDurationMs": 4760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And remember, start learning\nwhatever you want to learn this Diwali."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 197240,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Hello, friends!"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 198240,
    "dDurationMs": 1600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "To find the answer\nto this question,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 199840,
    "dDurationMs": 2300,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "we first have to\ndive under our feet."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 202140,
    "dDurationMs": 1500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The earth below us"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 203640,
    "dDurationMs": 1600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "has mainly four layers."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 205240,
    "dDurationMs": 1260,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The crust at the top,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 206500,
    "dDurationMs": 1240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "then the mantle,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 207740,
    "dDurationMs": 1060,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "then the outer core,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 208800,
    "dDurationMs": 1380,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and finally the inner core."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 210180,
    "dDurationMs": 4160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The outer core is\napproximately 2,250 km thick."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 214340,
    "dDurationMs": 2600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And it is made of\nmelted iron and nickel."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 216940,
    "dDurationMs": 3500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That is, at a depth of approximately\n2,900 km under our feet,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 220440,
    "dDurationMs": 2740,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "there is an entire\nsea of melted iron."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 223180,
    "dDurationMs": 2400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And this sea does not\njust stay in one place,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 225580,
    "dDurationMs": 2420,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but it keeps on rotating."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 228000,
    "dDurationMs": 2000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Electric currents\nare created by this."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 230000,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "According to NASA, these\ncurrents are hundreds of miles wide."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 233000,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And flow at a rate of\nthousands of miles per hour."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 236000,
    "dDurationMs": 2000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "As you must have read in school,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 238000,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "electric currents always\ncreate a magnetic field."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 241000,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So, these currents\nthat flow in the earth"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 244000,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "create the magnetic\nfield of the earth."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 247000,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This is what gives the\nearth its geomagnetic field."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 251000,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It is drawn in school\nbooks in such a way"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 254000,
    "dDurationMs": 2000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that it looks like there\nis a magnet in the earth."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 256000,
    "dDurationMs": 2400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But there is no\nmagnet present there."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 258400,
    "dDurationMs": 2640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It is actually the\nmelted iron in the earth"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 261040,
    "dDurationMs": 2000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that is making\nthe magnetic field."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 263040,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And this magnetic field\nworks like an invisible shield."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 267040,
    "dDurationMs": 4400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It protects us from the dangerous\nradiation from the sun and space."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 271440,
    "dDurationMs": 2880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This magnetic field has\na North and South Pole."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 274320,
    "dDurationMs": 3600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And the biggest clue to\nwhat is going on in the earth"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 277920,
    "dDurationMs": 1200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is this point."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 280720,
    "dDurationMs": 2640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now, here, a common\nmisconception is that"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 283360,
    "dDurationMs": 5000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "people confuse this magnetic North\nPole with Earth's geographic North Pole."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 288360,
    "dDurationMs": 5000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "People think that this\nis the only North Pole."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 293360,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But actually, the Earth\nhas two North Poles."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 296360,
    "dDurationMs": 2000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The first is the\nGeographic North Pole."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 298360,
    "dDurationMs": 2000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This is actually\nthe true North Pole."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 300360,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The northernmost point of the\nEarth, located in the Arctic Ocean."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 303360,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It is a fixed point."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 304360,
    "dDurationMs": 2000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The second is the\nMagnetic North Pole."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 306360,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Visually, this is the\nplace where the Earth's"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 309360,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "magnetic field lines go\ndirectly into the Earth."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 312360,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And when you use a\ncompass, whether it"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 315360,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is a hand compass\nor a phone compass,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 318360,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you can see the\nnorth on the compass."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 321360,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The north the compass is showing\nis actually the magnetic North Pole."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 325360,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But do you know that the magnetic\nNorth Pole never stays in one place?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 329975,
    "dDurationMs": 5000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It makes an elliptical path\nof about 120 km every day."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 335000,
    "dDurationMs": 3360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That is, the point that your\ncompass was pointing at this morning,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 338360,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that point has been dragged\nsomewhere else by the evening."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 341360,
    "dDurationMs": 1615,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And here is another\ninteresting fact."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 343000,
    "dDurationMs": 4280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The magnetic North Pole is\ntechnically a magnetic South Pole."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 347280,
    "dDurationMs": 2160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The compass needle\nis a small magnet."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 349440,
    "dDurationMs": 4080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You must have read\nthat opposite poles attract."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 353520,
    "dDurationMs": 3560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "One magnet's North Pole\nattracts the other's South Pole."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 357080,
    "dDurationMs": 3550,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The magnetic North Pole\nof the compass magnet is"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 360630,
    "dDurationMs": 3550,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "attracted to the magnetic\nSouth Pole of the Earth."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 364180,
    "dDurationMs": 2000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That is why it is\ntechnically the opposite."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 366180,
    "dDurationMs": 4140,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But to keep things simple, we\ncall it the magnetic North Pole."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 370320,
    "dDurationMs": 3800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now the question is, why does this\nmagnetic North Pole keep moving?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 374120,
    "dDurationMs": 3480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "To find out the answer to this,\nwe have to go back 200 years."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 377600,
    "dDurationMs": 3280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In the Arctic region of Canada, there\nis a place called the Boothia Peninsula."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 380880,
    "dDurationMs": 1760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Not Bhootia, but Boothia."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 382640,
    "dDurationMs": 5680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In 1831, the British explorer James\nClark Ross's ship got stuck in the ice."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 388320,
    "dDurationMs": 2000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "He had a magnetic needle,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 390320,
    "dDurationMs": 2000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which was strung on a silk thread."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 392320,
    "dDurationMs": 2720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And he was looking\nfor a very specific place."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 395040,
    "dDurationMs": 5360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The point where this needle\nwould point downwards."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 400560,
    "dDurationMs": 2020,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That is, the\nMagnetic North Pole."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 402660,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "After searching for many days, they\nfinally found this place on June 1st, 1831."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 408040,
    "dDurationMs": 2540,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "As soon as they found\nthis point, Ross made a"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 410580,
    "dDurationMs": 3408,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "pile of stones there and\nraised the British flag."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 414120,
    "dDurationMs": 2915,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "He immediately\ndeclared it British territory."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 417060,
    "dDurationMs": 2080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Because he was the\nfirst person to reach here."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 419140,
    "dDurationMs": 4190,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But surprisingly, this\nmagnetic North Pole"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 423330,
    "dDurationMs": 4190,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "was about 1,600 km south\nof the Geographic North Pole."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 427520,
    "dDurationMs": 2810,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You might think that both\nthese North Poles are very"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 430330,
    "dDurationMs": 2810,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "close to each other, but\nthey were 1,600 km away."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 433140,
    "dDurationMs": 3198,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And this was when\nthe flag was raised."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 436433,
    "dDurationMs": 3707,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "After this, this pole started\nto shift from its place."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 443140,
    "dDurationMs": 2590,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In the beginning, it moved slowly."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 445809,
    "dDurationMs": 7307,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "From 1904 to 1990, it moved on\naverage only 9 to 15 km per year."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 453140,
    "dDurationMs": 2860,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That is, every day, it\nmoved only 25 to 40 meters."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 456000,
    "dDurationMs": 2000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "About the length of\ntwo cricket pitches."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 458000,
    "dDurationMs": 3606,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But around 1990, something\nhappened that caused"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 461630,
    "dDurationMs": 3370,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "this magnetic North\nPole to pick up speed."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 465000,
    "dDurationMs": 4668,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Instead of shifting slowly,\nit almost started to run."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 469715,
    "dDurationMs": 3285,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In 1990, it moved at a\nspeed of 55 km per year."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 473025,
    "dDurationMs": 3482,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That means it was sliding\nabout 150 meters every day."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 476586,
    "dDurationMs": 5942,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Between 1990 and 2005, its\nspeed was 50 to 60 km per year."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 482600,
    "dDurationMs": 3840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In just a few years, its speed\nhad increased four times."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 486440,
    "dDurationMs": 3400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "By the year 2000, it had\nleft the land of Canada"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 489840,
    "dDurationMs": 2200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and crossed over from\nthe Western Hemisphere."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 492040,
    "dDurationMs": 6740,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In October 2017, it was only 390 km\naway from the Geographic North Pole."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 498780,
    "dDurationMs": 2800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Today, the magnetic North\nPole is in the Eastern Hemisphere,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 501580,
    "dDurationMs": 2860,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and is moving\ntowards Siberia, Russia."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 504440,
    "dDurationMs": 2100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If you want to understand\nit in the Indian context,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 506540,
    "dDurationMs": 3280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "think of it as if the magnetic\nNorth Pole was in Delhi before,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 509820,
    "dDurationMs": 3320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and has now advanced\nbeyond Kanyakumari."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 513140,
    "dDurationMs": 2500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This is the reason why\non February 4, 2019,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 515640,
    "dDurationMs": 5220,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "American scientists issued an emergency\nupdate on the World Magnetic Model."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 520860,
    "dDurationMs": 3140,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This is the model that tracks\nthe magnetic field of the Earth,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 524000,
    "dDurationMs": 2660,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and is used for navigation\nby ships and aircraft,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 526660,
    "dDurationMs": 3300,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "as well as Google Maps."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 529960,
    "dDurationMs": 3040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This model is usually\nupdated once every 5 years."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 533000,
    "dDurationMs": 3700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But this time, it had to be\nupdated 10 months earlier."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 536700,
    "dDurationMs": 3440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Because the magnetic North\nPole was shifting so rapidly"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 540140,
    "dDurationMs": 2420,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that the world map\nwas becoming incorrect."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 542560,
    "dDurationMs": 1740,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You might wonder,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 544300,
    "dDurationMs": 3540,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "if an invisible point is\nslipping under the ice,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 547840,
    "dDurationMs": 1900,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "what difference\ndoes it make to us?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 549740,
    "dDurationMs": 2000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In reality, it makes\na huge difference."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 551740,
    "dDurationMs": 2720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And the most visible\nexample is airports."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 554460,
    "dDurationMs": 2420,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The names of the runways\nin airports around the world"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 556880,
    "dDurationMs": 1460,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "are designated with numbers."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 558340,
    "dDurationMs": 2280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "18, 27, 36."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 560620,
    "dDurationMs": 1680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "These numbers are not random."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 562300,
    "dDurationMs": 2240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They come from the compass\nheading of the runway."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 564540,
    "dDurationMs": 4718,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "For example, 18 means it is pointing\n180 degrees according to the compass."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 569322,
    "dDurationMs": 3178,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If the magnetic north shifts,\nthe real compass heading"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 572500,
    "dDurationMs": 2500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of the runway and its\nnumber will be different."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 575000,
    "dDurationMs": 3500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "For example, if a plane\nwants to land on runway 18, it"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 578500,
    "dDurationMs": 3500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "means that the plane has to\ncome on a 180 degree heading."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 582000,
    "dDurationMs": 3500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But if the magnetic North Pole\ndirection has changed, then"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 585500,
    "dDurationMs": 3500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that 180 degree heading can\ngo in a slightly different direction."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 589000,
    "dDurationMs": 5000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "When it changes significantly, airports\nhave to update the names of the runways."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 594000,
    "dDurationMs": 3780,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In 2009, the Fairbanks\nInternational Airport in Alaska"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 597780,
    "dDurationMs": 5660,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "had to change its runway\nname from 1L-19R to 2L-20R."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 603440,
    "dDurationMs": 2440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And at the speed at which\nthe North Pole is moving,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 605880,
    "dDurationMs": 4440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it is estimated that it will have to\nchange its name again around 2033."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 610320,
    "dDurationMs": 2200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But this is not limited\nonly to airports."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 612520,
    "dDurationMs": 2300,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It also affects your daily life."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 614820,
    "dDurationMs": 3180,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Google Maps takes\nyour location from GPS."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 618000,
    "dDurationMs": 2200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But which way you are facing"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 620200,
    "dDurationMs": 2200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is shown by the\ncompass of your phone."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 622400,
    "dDurationMs": 3220,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That means if the magnetic\nNorth Pole is moving, and"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 625620,
    "dDurationMs": 3613,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the model is not updated, the\ncompass will show the wrong direction."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 629320,
    "dDurationMs": 2660,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And most importantly,\nit will also affect the"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 631980,
    "dDurationMs": 2660,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "navigation systems of the\nmilitaries of all countries."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 634800,
    "dDurationMs": 3277,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So, roughly speaking,\nit has a very big impact."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 638140,
    "dDurationMs": 3927,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But now the question is, why is\nthe North Pole moving so much?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 642413,
    "dDurationMs": 2174,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And at an increasing speed."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 644667,
    "dDurationMs": 2593,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now, as I told you, this\nmagnetic North Pole is the"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 647260,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "result of melted iron in\nthe outer core of the earth."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 650260,
    "dDurationMs": 5280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If this pole is flowing so fast, it means\nthat something is changing below."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 655540,
    "dDurationMs": 4320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "We cannot directly see\nwhat is changing below,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 659860,
    "dDurationMs": 5280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "because we do not have any machine\nthat can go 3,000 km below the Earth."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 665140,
    "dDurationMs": 3760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "We have the answer\nfrom satellites."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 669552,
    "dDurationMs": 3223,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In May 2020, Philip\nLivermore and his colleagues"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 672799,
    "dDurationMs": 2741,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "published a paper in\nNature Geoscience."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 675540,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And in this paper,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 676540,
    "dDurationMs": 2700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "using 20 years\nof satellite data,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 679240,
    "dDurationMs": 2680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the reason for this whole\npuzzle was explained."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 681920,
    "dDurationMs": 2080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "He said that in the Earth,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 684000,
    "dDurationMs": 3500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "on the boundary of the mantle and the outer\ncore, the magnetic field is not uniform."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 687500,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And there are two large lobes where\nthe magnetic field is concentrated."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 691500,
    "dDurationMs": 3500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "One of these lobes is below\nCanada and the other below Siberia."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 695000,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Between these two lobes,\nthere is a tug of war going on."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 698000,
    "dDurationMs": 4500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And both are pulling the magnetic\nNorth Pole towards themselves."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 702500,
    "dDurationMs": 3500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now, when these two were equally\nstrong, the pole was stuck between them."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 706000,
    "dDurationMs": 3500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But between 1970 and\n1999, the pattern of the"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 709500,
    "dDurationMs": 3500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "flow of iron in the\nouter core changed."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 713000,
    "dDurationMs": 3840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And that change made\nthe Canada lobe elongated."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 716840,
    "dDurationMs": 2040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Because it stretched,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 718880,
    "dDurationMs": 3460,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "its strength was no longer\nconcentrated in one place."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 722340,
    "dDurationMs": 1200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It started to weaken."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 723540,
    "dDurationMs": 3100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And when the magnetic\nlobe below Canada weakened,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 726640,
    "dDurationMs": 3640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the actual magnetic North Pole"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 730280,
    "dDurationMs": 1920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "shifted towards Siberia."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 732200,
    "dDurationMs": 3080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now, you might not\nfind this very interesting,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 735280,
    "dDurationMs": 3480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but the problem is that this\nis where the real fear begins."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 738760,
    "dDurationMs": 3580,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Because sometimes, this\ntug of war gets so extreme"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 742340,
    "dDurationMs": 3040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that these magnetic poles flip."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 745380,
    "dDurationMs": 1800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And this has happened before,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 747180,
    "dDurationMs": 1600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "hundreds of times."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 750540,
    "dDurationMs": 3320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In 1905, a French\nphysicist, Bernard Brunhes,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 753860,
    "dDurationMs": 5000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "found something very interesting\nin a village called Pontfarein."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 758860,
    "dDurationMs": 2240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "During digging for a road,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 761100,
    "dDurationMs": 5280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a layer of lava was found right\nabove the terracotta, or solid soil."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 766380,
    "dDurationMs": 2200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Brunhes was looking for\nthat specific layer of soil."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 768580,
    "dDurationMs": 2000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Because when lava\nflows and cools down,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 770580,
    "dDurationMs": 2000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the magnetic particles inside it"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 772580,
    "dDurationMs": 3420,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "freeze in the direction of\nthe magnetic field at that time."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 776000,
    "dDurationMs": 2700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This soil had become\na stone compass."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 778700,
    "dDurationMs": 2940,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "A compass that had\nrecords of the magnetic"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 781640,
    "dDurationMs": 2940,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "fields from hundreds of\nthousands of years ago."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 784580,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So Brunhes took it to his\nlab and conducted research."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 787580,
    "dDurationMs": 2000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "After the research,\nhe found that"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 789580,
    "dDurationMs": 3420,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the magnetic\ndirection inside this soil"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 793000,
    "dDurationMs": 3420,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "was the opposite of\nthe current direction."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 796420,
    "dDurationMs": 1580,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That is, at that time,\nthe magnetic North Pole"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 798000,
    "dDurationMs": 2520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "was the magnetic South Pole,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 800520,
    "dDurationMs": 3160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and the magnetic South Pole\nwas the magnetic North Pole."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 803680,
    "dDurationMs": 2560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But at that time, this\nclaim was so sensational"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 806240,
    "dDurationMs": 3280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that scientists made\nfun of it for decades."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 809520,
    "dDurationMs": 2360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They could not\nbelieve his research,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 811880,
    "dDurationMs": 2760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "thinking that this\nwas impossible."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 814640,
    "dDurationMs": 1680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But in 1960,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 816320,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a map of the ocean\nproved Brunhes right."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 820320,
    "dDurationMs": 2880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "At that time, magnetometers\nwere towed behind ships"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 823200,
    "dDurationMs": 1840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to perform seabed surveys."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 825040,
    "dDurationMs": 3700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And they found a pattern of\nmagnetic lines on the seabed"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 828740,
    "dDurationMs": 2700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that matched the\nstripes on a zebra."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 831440,
    "dDurationMs": 3340,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "These lines were the record of the\nchanging magnetic field of the earth."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 834780,
    "dDurationMs": 2500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That is, sometimes the\ndirection of the field was one way,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 837280,
    "dDurationMs": 2000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and sometimes the opposite."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 839280,
    "dDurationMs": 1580,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And the most\nsurprising thing was that"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 840860,
    "dDurationMs": 1740,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "these lines on both\nsides of the ridge"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 842600,
    "dDurationMs": 2200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "were mirror images\nof each other."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 844800,
    "dDurationMs": 2520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "On the ridges below the sea,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 847320,
    "dDurationMs": 2920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the tectonic plates of the earth\nkeep moving away from each other."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 850240,
    "dDurationMs": 3500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And new lava comes up from\nthe empty areas between them."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 853740,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The lava keeps filling up and\ncools down in the sea water."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 857740,
    "dDurationMs": 4350,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But even here, the\nlava records the direction"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 862090,
    "dDurationMs": 4350,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of the magnetic field\nthrough the magnetic minerals."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 866440,
    "dDurationMs": 4020,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The seabed under the sea was\nalso working like a tape recorder,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 870460,
    "dDurationMs": 4480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "on which every magnetic\nflip of the Earth was recorded."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 874940,
    "dDurationMs": 3040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "When scientists observed\nand investigated this,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 877980,
    "dDurationMs": 5640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "this tape recorder revealed the\nentire magnetic history of the Earth."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 887620,
    "dDurationMs": 2640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And the data they found here"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 890260,
    "dDurationMs": 2560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "shocked everyone."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 892820,
    "dDurationMs": 2480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "After seeing them,\nscientists understood that"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 895300,
    "dDurationMs": 2760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "these zebra like lines were caused\nby the magnetic field of the Earth"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 898060,
    "dDurationMs": 1800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "being flipped over\nand over again."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 899860,
    "dDurationMs": 3080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Whether it is the Pacific Ocean, the\nAtlantic Ocean, or the Indian Ocean,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 902940,
    "dDurationMs": 3840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the same patterns were seen\neverywhere under the sea."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 906780,
    "dDurationMs": 5220,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Magnetic flips have occurred\nacross the entire earth."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 912000,
    "dDurationMs": 2640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Scientists found that in\nthe last 80 million years,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 914640,
    "dDurationMs": 3680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "magnetic poles have\nflipped 183 times."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 918320,
    "dDurationMs": 3660,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "On average, every 430,000 years,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 921980,
    "dDurationMs": 3140,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the magnetic poles change."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 925120,
    "dDurationMs": 1360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Listen to this carefully."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 926480,
    "dDurationMs": 2160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Every 400,000 years, on average,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 928640,
    "dDurationMs": 3360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the magnetic North Pole and\nmagnetic South Pole of the Earth"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 932000,
    "dDurationMs": 1320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "flip."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 933320,
    "dDurationMs": 1520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And the most shocking thing,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 934840,
    "dDurationMs": 4100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the last flip happened\n780,000 years ago."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 938940,
    "dDurationMs": 3560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now you might wonder, if\nthe last flip was so far back,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 942500,
    "dDurationMs": 2640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "then the event I talked about\nat the beginning of the video"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 945140,
    "dDurationMs": 2280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "was only 42,000 years ago."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 947420,
    "dDurationMs": 1960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "What happened then?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 949380,
    "dDurationMs": 2480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Actually, a temporary\nflip took place."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 951860,
    "dDurationMs": 2820,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The magnetic poles\nhad temporarily reversed"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 954680,
    "dDurationMs": 1520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "for a short time,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 956200,
    "dDurationMs": 1900,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and then returned to\ntheir original places."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 958100,
    "dDurationMs": 3800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This event is called the Laschamp\nExcursion in scientific terms."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 961900,
    "dDurationMs": 2920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This was the time\nwhen both the magnetic"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 964820,
    "dDurationMs": 2920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "poles had changed\nplaces for about 800 years."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 967740,
    "dDurationMs": 2740,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But then they returned\nto their original positions."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 970480,
    "dDurationMs": 3040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In 2021, a study published\nin the journal Science"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 973520,
    "dDurationMs": 3280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "showed that the magnetic field\nstrength of the Earth at that time"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 976800,
    "dDurationMs": 2540,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "was only 0 to 6%."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 979340,
    "dDurationMs": 3320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That means the magnetic\nfield of the Earth was very weak."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 982660,
    "dDurationMs": 4200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "We had almost\nno invisible shield."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 986860,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "We had nothing to protect ourselves\nfrom the dangerous radiation from space."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 991420,
    "dDurationMs": 2460,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In this 2021 study,\nit was suggested that"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 993880,
    "dDurationMs": 3420,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the Neanderthals of Europe\nalso died because of this."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 997300,
    "dDurationMs": 2760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The entirety of a human-like species,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1000060,
    "dDurationMs": 3680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "went extinct because\nof this one event."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1003740,
    "dDurationMs": 2880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "At the same time, the\nozone layer was destroyed."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1006620,
    "dDurationMs": 3680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And many species of animals\nand plants became extinct."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1010300,
    "dDurationMs": 4180,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Like the giant kangaroo\nspecies in Australia."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1014480,
    "dDurationMs": 4240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This research paper connects\nall these incidents with this flip."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1018720,
    "dDurationMs": 2100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And this is the\nreason why in 2019,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1020820,
    "dDurationMs": 2300,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "when the news broke of the\nmoving magnetic North Pole,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1023120,
    "dDurationMs": 3249,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "there were claims on the internet\nthat the poles were going to reverse."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1026408,
    "dDurationMs": 2267,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That the Earth's magnetic\nfield might disappear."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1028700,
    "dDurationMs": 3840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It was also claimed that when\nthe poles reversed for a while,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1032540,
    "dDurationMs": 3300,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a whole species of humans\ndisappeared from the Earth."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1037680,
    "dDurationMs": 3680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So the question is, will we also\ndisappear like the Neanderthals?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1041360,
    "dDurationMs": 3560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And even more importantly,\nwhen will the next flip take place?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1044920,
    "dDurationMs": 3600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Many researchers believe\nthat the next flip is long overdue."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1048520,
    "dDurationMs": 4460,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Because on average, every 430,000\nyears, these poles have flipped."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1052980,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And the last flip happened\n780,000 years ago."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1055980,
    "dDurationMs": 4240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Two Italian researchers\nhave given a point of no return."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1060220,
    "dDurationMs": 2240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The year 2034,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1062460,
    "dDurationMs": 1400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "plus or minus 3 years."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1063860,
    "dDurationMs": 2400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "According to them, after 2034,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1066260,
    "dDurationMs": 3080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a flip of the Earth's magnetic\nfield would be inevitable."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1069340,
    "dDurationMs": 4120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But other scientists say that there\nis no fixed schedule for the flip."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1073460,
    "dDurationMs": 2320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "430,000 years is\njust an average."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1075780,
    "dDurationMs": 2040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And these flips are random."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1077820,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It can take 10,000\nyears or 50 million years."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1082700,
    "dDurationMs": 3360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Between 118 million years ago,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1086060,
    "dDurationMs": 2760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and 83 million years ago,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1088820,
    "dDurationMs": 2640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "when there was no\nmagnetic flip for long periods."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1091460,
    "dDurationMs": 3380,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Another thing to note is that\nthese flips are not sudden."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1094840,
    "dDurationMs": 2600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It is not like you wake up\nin the morning and find that"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1097440,
    "dDurationMs": 2040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the magnetic poles have flipped."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1099480,
    "dDurationMs": 1620,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "To complete the last flip,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1101100,
    "dDurationMs": 4220,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it took from 1,000 to 10,000 years\naccording to different estimates."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1105320,
    "dDurationMs": 2240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If the flip starts today,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1107560,
    "dDurationMs": 3280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the lives of your children\nand your children's children"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1110840,
    "dDurationMs": 2160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "will pass long before the\nflip process completes."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1113000,
    "dDurationMs": 2960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And as for how weak the\nmagnetic field will be when it flips,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1115960,
    "dDurationMs": 3840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and how harmful it will be\nto humans and other animals,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1119800,
    "dDurationMs": 2880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "we don't need to worry much about it."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1122680,
    "dDurationMs": 1840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "According to\nNASA, during a flip,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1124520,
    "dDurationMs": 2000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the magnetic field only weakens."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1126520,
    "dDurationMs": 1680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It does not\ncompletely disappear."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1128200,
    "dDurationMs": 1440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "According to most scientists,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1129640,
    "dDurationMs": 2640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "during the flip, the\nmagnetic field's strength"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1132280,
    "dDurationMs": 2160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "drops by about 25%."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1134440,
    "dDurationMs": 2480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The event that took place\nin the Laschamp Excursion,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1136920,
    "dDurationMs": 3080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "where only 5% of the strength\nof the magnetic field remained,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1140000,
    "dDurationMs": 2000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "was a very extreme case."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1142000,
    "dDurationMs": 2000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Most flips are not like that."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1144000,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And similarly, there is\nno solid evidence that"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1147000,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a magnetic pole flip can\ncause mass extinction."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1151000,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The 2021 study in which\nthat claim was made"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1154000,
    "dDurationMs": 2000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "has been constantly questioned."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1156000,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That same year, 10 scientists\npublished another study,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1159000,
    "dDurationMs": 2000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "according to which"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1161000,
    "dDurationMs": 2500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "there is no proven\nevidence of the extinction of"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1163500,
    "dDurationMs": 3017,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Neanderthals and other species\nbecause of the Laschamp event."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1166541,
    "dDurationMs": 2000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "During the last big pole flips,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1168541,
    "dDurationMs": 2500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "there was no major\nchange seen in the fossils"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1171041,
    "dDurationMs": 2500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of the plants and\nanimals of that time."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1173541,
    "dDurationMs": 2710,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Nor has there been\nany mass extinction."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1176276,
    "dDurationMs": 2362,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So the thing is that research\nis still ongoing on this."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1178663,
    "dDurationMs": 2878,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Nothing can be stated\nwith absolute certainty."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1181541,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Yes, one thing is for sure: those animal\nspecies will definitely suffer losses"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1185541,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that navigate with the\nhelp of magnetic fields."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1188541,
    "dDurationMs": 5000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Like whales, butterflies, sea\nturtles, and migratory birds."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1193541,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "These sea turtles travel\nthousands of kilometres to lay"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1196541,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "eggs on the same beach\nwhere they were born."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1199541,
    "dDurationMs": 5416,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And they identify the beach with\nthe help of its magnetic signature."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1205019,
    "dDurationMs": 4497,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So it can be said that the next\ntime the magnetic poles flip,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1209541,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "there will be a huge impact on\nthe species of all these animals."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1215333,
    "dDurationMs": 3627,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Thankfully, we do not live\nin jungles and caves today."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1218985,
    "dDurationMs": 2381,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If cosmic radiation increases,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1221367,
    "dDurationMs": 2000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and the magnetic field weakens,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1223367,
    "dDurationMs": 2560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "we can take shelter\nin our buildings,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1225927,
    "dDurationMs": 1760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "we can take\nshelter in our homes."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1227687,
    "dDurationMs": 2720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Actually, the biggest\nthreat is something"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1230407,
    "dDurationMs": 3520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which was not present on\nEarth during previous pole flips."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1233927,
    "dDurationMs": 3120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And that thing is\nmodern technology."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1238727,
    "dDurationMs": 3840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The majority of today's technology\nis based on electromagnetic fields."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1242567,
    "dDurationMs": 3200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And any major change\nin electromagnetic fields"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1245767,
    "dDurationMs": 3280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "can impact this\ntechnology on a large scale,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1249047,
    "dDurationMs": 1560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "especially satellites."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1250607,
    "dDurationMs": 1800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now, what all can happen here"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1252407,
    "dDurationMs": 2703,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "can be seen in the reflection\nof the Bermuda Triangle"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1255135,
    "dDurationMs": 2000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "between South\nAmerica and Africa,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1257135,
    "dDurationMs": 3175,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the region where the magnetic\nfield on Earth is a little weak,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1260335,
    "dDurationMs": 4635,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and radiation coming from space\nreaches the satellites there more easily."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1265049,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This is why data from telescopes\nlike the Hubble starts to get glitches."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1269049,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And that region in space is called\nthe Bermuda Triangle of Space."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1273049,
    "dDurationMs": 2500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now think about\nit, if during a flip the"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1275549,
    "dDurationMs": 2500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "magnetic field on the\nentire Earth becomes weak,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1278049,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "then this Bermuda Triangle will\nnot only be limited to one region"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1281049,
    "dDurationMs": 2000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but will spread\nall over the Earth."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1283049,
    "dDurationMs": 3500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The good news is that\nthere is no evidence"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1286549,
    "dDurationMs": 3500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that the magnetic North\nPole is actually flipping today."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1290049,
    "dDurationMs": 5000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And the shift that is happening is not\nhappening because the world is ending."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1295049,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It is shifting because it has\nnever stayed in one place."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1299049,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Today, in 2026, its\nspeed has also decreased."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1302049,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The magnetic North\nPole, which was moving at"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1305049,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "50 to 60 km per\nyear toward Siberia,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1308049,
    "dDurationMs": 5000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "now has a speed that has\ndecreased to only 35 to 36 km per year."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1313049,
    "dDurationMs": 2600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This is something that\nhas changed over time."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1315649,
    "dDurationMs": 3420,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The question is, will\nhumans be present to"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1319069,
    "dDurationMs": 3420,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "see the moment the\npoles flip next time?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1322489,
    "dDurationMs": 3920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Or will they have already\nfinished themselves before then?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1328169,
    "dDurationMs": 3140,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now, if you want to\nknow what happened"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1331309,
    "dDurationMs": 3140,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to the other species of\nhumans, like Neanderthals,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1334449,
    "dDurationMs": 2160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and how they became extinct,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1336609,
    "dDurationMs": 3760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I have explained that\nin detail in this video."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1340369,
    "dDurationMs": 1640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You can click here to watch it."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1342009,
    "dDurationMs": 2880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And don't forget to take advantage of\nthe Diwali sale on Dhruv Rathee Academy."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1345009,
    "dDurationMs": 2895,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Flat 50% off on every course."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1347929,
    "dDurationMs": 1904,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You can click here and join."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1349889,
    "dDurationMs": 1411,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Thank you very much!"
    } ]
  } ]
}
